1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,820
I think social media can motivate and encourage you to become better,

2
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:07,860
just like I said earlier.

3
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:12,040
You see a video and think, “Wow, they can do that. I can't. I'd love to be able to do that too.”

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:16,720
That can be a positive influence, but I'd make sure that

5
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:24,240
I don't take more risk than I normally would just for the sake of a video.

6
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:31,940
In general, I'd also say you shouldn't try to do too much too quickly. I mean,

7
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:36,660
in my case, I started when I was 20, so I never felt any pressure.

8
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:41,380
I always thought I still had plenty of time. I didn't need to rush anything.

9
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:48,040
Slow progression is safe progression,

10
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:52,700
and I think you should enjoy every step along the way. If you do

11
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:57,980
20 jumps in a two piece tracking suit just to move straight into a wingsuit,

12
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:02,840
you miss out on all the fun you could have had without a suit, or with a two piece,

13
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:06,520
or with a one piece tracking suit. It's all a lot of fun, and they're all

14
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:10,880
important skills that help make you a good wingsuit BASE jumper later on.

15
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:16,820
Take it slowly, experience everything, do lots of easy jumps, and choose the days

16
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:20,920
when you push yourself and approach your limits very carefully.

17
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:27,320
Because if you want to improve, you do have to push your limits from time to time.

18
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:33,200
You just have to do it safely, pick the right days, and not do it every

19
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:37,920
single day, because otherwise an accident will happen sooner or later, and that's something you want to avoid.
